body:
The only missing piece for a real VENC encode is the client buffer PA. V41 now accepts pa-only registration; the daemon needs to read pa for a client handle. Exact minimal change, for your approval:

include/redwood_vcodec.h (frozen -> you edit):
  /* RWVC_DMA_INFO: minor 0 (server) asks for the physical address of a DMA handle that a minor-1 client
   * allocated with the share flag.  Same access rule as RWVC_DMA_RW: only the other minor may inspect it. */
  struct rwvc_dma_info { uint32_t handle, bytes, out_pa, reserved; };
  #define RWVC_DMA_INFO RWVC_IOC(0xc0000000u, 12, struct rwvc_dma_info)

K02: fill out_pa from the pool table only when the handle exists and is shared to minor 0; bytes = its size;
  ENOENT unknown, EPERM not shared, EINVAL handle 0.  No new pool state, no copy.
IK: allow the ioctl on both minors with that rule (the server is the normal caller).
vcodecd (me): on the first ENC_FRAME that names a handle, ioctl it once, then n2vc_dma_guest_register(h, NULL, handle, pa, bytes, NULL);
  n2vc_dma_guest_forget(handle) when the session ends or the client reuses a handle.  No protocol change, no new client API.
I will implement as soon as the header has the name/layout; I did not add a private ioctl number because that would fork the ABI.

If you prefer a different shape (e.g. two handles per call, or a P03 function), tell me the exact signature and I will code that instead. Until then a real ENC_FRAME answers E_ARGS after V41 rejects pa=0; the host suite is 627/627 and this is the first phone blocker.
